927.6813zm1.0976-2.3654 2.602-1.4998 2.6069 1.4998v2.9994l-2.5974 1.4997-2.6067-1.4997Z\"></path></svg>Codex</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Availability</td><td>Conductor includes a managed Codex executable. You can use your own Codex install instead.</td></tr><tr><td>Setup</td><td>Codex sign-in or API-key access from the workspace environment.</td></tr><tr><td>Models</td><td>Codex models visible to the active OpenAI account and Codex setup.</td></tr><tr><td>Billing</td><td>OpenAI subscription, ChatGPT credits, or API-key billing.</td></tr><tr><td>Controls</td><td>Plan Mode, Fast Mode, goals, reasoning controls, personalities, checkpoints, and skills where supported.</td></tr></tbody></table></section></div><h2 id=\"setup-notes\"><a href=\"#setup-notes\">Setup notes</a></h2><p>Conductor can use the bundled Codex binary or a configured system Codex binary.</p><p>Codex auth can come from Codex CLI sign-in outside Conductor or from API-key based access. For setup examples, see <a href=\"/docs/guides/providers#codex\">Configure model providers: Codex</a>.</p><h2 id=\"model-access\"><a href=\"#model-access\">Model access</a></h2><p>The models visible in Conductor depend on your Codex setup, account, subscription, API access, and model availability when you start the session.</p>",
  "text": "Codex is OpenAI's coding harness for interacting with GPT-series models. Conductor comes with Codex preinstalled and allows you to use an OpenAI API key or existing subscription.\nCodex quick facts\nOpenAI Codex model docsTopicCodexAvailabilityConductor includes a managed Codex executable. You can use your own Codex install instead.SetupCodex sign-in or API-key access from the workspace environment.ModelsCodex models visible to the active OpenAI account and Codex setup.BillingOpenAI subscription, ChatGPT credits, or API-key billing.ControlsPlan Mode, Fast Mode, goals, reasoning controls, personalities, checkpoints, and skills where supported.Setup notes\nConductor can use the bundled Codex binary or a configured system Codex binary.\nCodex auth can come from Codex CLI sign-in outside Conductor or from API-key based access. For setup examples, see Configure model providers: Codex.\nModel access\nThe models visible in Conductor depend on your Codex setup, account, subscription, API access, and model availability when you start the session.",
  "markdown": "\n# Codex\n\n\n\nCodex is OpenAI's coding harness for interacting with GPT-series models. Conductor comes with Codex preinstalled and allows you to use an OpenAI API key or existing subscription.\n\n\n\n\n## Setup notes [#setup-notes]\n\nConductor can use the bundled Codex binary or a configured system Codex binary.\n\nCodex auth can come from Codex CLI sign-in outside Conductor or from API-key based access. For setup examples, see [Configure model providers: Codex](/docs/guides/providers#codex).\n\n## Model access [#model-access]\n\nThe models visible in Conductor depend on your Codex setup, account, subscription, API access, and model availability when you start the session.\n"
}
